The expected value of a random variable $X$ taking values $X_1,X_2,\dots$ is $E[X]=\sum_k X_k\Pr[X=X_k]$. Two random variables are independent ($X\perp Y$) if $\Pr[(X=a)\cap(Y=b)]=\Pr[X=a]\Pr[Y=b]$ for all $a,b$.

Prove the following properties of expected value, for random variables $X,Y$ with finite expectations and a constant $c$:
- $E[cX]=cE[X]$ and $E[c+X]=c+E[X]$;
- $E[XY]=E[X]E[Y]$ if $X\perp Y$;
- (linearity) $E[X+Y]=E[X]+E[Y]$.
